### ─── Exportable Reports (PMS-014) ──────────────────────────────────────────
### Uses the REST Client extension (humao.rest-client).
###
### Quick start:
###   1. Start the API:  npm start   (and the DB: npm run db:up)
###   2. Send "Login as Admin" (and optionally "Login as Pharmacist") below.
###   3. Send a "request" — small ranges come back as a FILE (200); big ones as
###      a queued job (202). Then poll status and download.
###
### All authenticated routes require a Bearer access token and ADMIN or
### PHARMACIST role. A cashier gets 403.
###
### Endpoints covered:
###   POST  /reports                 Request a report (200 = inline file, 202 = queued)
###   GET   /reports                 List report jobs (paged, filterable)
###   GET   /reports/stream          SSE stream of YOUR report completions (admin sees all)
###   GET   /reports/:id             Get one report job's status
###   GET   /reports/:id/download    Download a completed file (needs Bearer — for the SPA)
###   GET   /reports/d/:token        Download via the signed email link (NO auth header)
###
### reportType: SALES_SUMMARY | SALES_DETAIL | INVENTORY_MOVEMENTS | STOCK_SNAPSHOT |
###             EXPIRY | PURCHASES | RETURNS
### format:     XLSX | PDF
### Optional filters: from, to (YYYY-MM-DD inclusive), timezone (IANA), productId,
###             lotId, movementType, userId, supplierId, horizonDays (EXPIRY only)

@host = http://localhost
@port = 3000
@base = {{host}}:{{port}}/api


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### AUTH — log in as admin (full access) and a cashier (to show 403).
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# @name loginAdmin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@openpharmacy.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### ── Login as Pharmacist ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @name loginPharmacist
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "pharmacist@openpharmacy.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### ── Login as Cashier (should be denied) ────────────────────────────────────
# @name loginCashier
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "cashier@openpharmacy.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### ── Store tokens for later requests ────────────────────────────────────────
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}
@pharmToken = {{loginPharmacist.response.body.accessToken}}
@cashierToken = {{loginCashier.response.body.accessToken}}

### Variables to fill in from previous responses:
@jobId = REPORT_JOB_UUID
@signedToken = PASTE_TOKEN_FROM_EMAIL_LINK


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SYNC REPORT — small range returns the file directly.
### Expect: 200 + application/vnd...sheet body (XLSX) and an
###         X-Report-Job-Id header. REST Client shows it as a binary download.
### (Whether a request is sync or async depends on the server's
###  REPORT_SYNC_THRESHOLD vs the estimated row count, not on the client.)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

POST {{base}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "reportType": "SALES_SUMMARY",
  "format": "XLSX",
  "from": "2025-01-01",
  "to": "2025-01-31",
  "timezone": "America/La_Paz"
}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SYNC REPORT — PDF variant.
### Expect: 200 + application/pdf (requires a Chromium binary on the server;
###         see REPORT_DOWNLOAD / puppeteer config).
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

POST {{base}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "reportType": "SALES_SUMMARY",
  "format": "PDF",
  "from": "2025-05-01",
  "to": "2025-05-31",
  "timezone": "America/La_Paz"
}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### ASYNC REPORT — large range is queued.
### Expect: 202 + { id, status: "QUEUED", ... }. When the worker finishes, the
###         user is notified via SSE and email; then GET /reports/:id/download.
### Copy .body.id into @jobId to follow up below.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# @name requestLargeReport
POST {{base}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "reportType": "INVENTORY_MOVEMENTS",
  "format": "XLSX",
  "from": "2025-01-01",
  "to": "2025-01-31"
}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### REQUEST EACH REPORT TYPE — filter bodies for exploration.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Sales detail (one row per sold line)
POST {{base}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "reportType": "SALES_DETAIL", "format": "XLSX", "from": "2025-01-01", "to": "2025-01-31" }

### Inventory movements, filtered by type
POST {{base}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "reportType": "INVENTORY_MOVEMENTS",
  "format": "XLSX",
  "from": "2025-01-01",
  "to": "2025-01-31",
  "movementType": "SALE"
}

### Stock snapshot + valuation (a point-in-time report; dates/horizon ignored)
POST {{base}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "reportType": "STOCK_SNAPSHOT", "format": "XLSX" }

### Expiry report — lots expiring within 90 days (horizonDays is optional)
POST {{base}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "reportType": "EXPIRY", "format": "XLSX", "horizonDays": 90 }

### Purchases (POs + receipt progress), optionally by supplier
POST {{base}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "reportType": "PURCHASES",
  "format": "XLSX",
  "from": "2025-01-01",
  "to": "2025-01-31",
  "supplierId": "SUPPLIER_UUID"
}

### Returns & cancellations
POST {{base}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "reportType": "RETURNS", "format": "XLSX", "from": "2025-01-01", "to": "2025-01-31" }


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### VALIDATION — unknown report type. Expect: 400 (ValidationPipe @IsEnum).
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

POST {{base}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "reportType": "MONTHLY_BOOST", "format": "XLSX" }


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### VALIDATION — over-long date range (> REPORT_MAX_RANGE_DAYS, default 366).
### Expect: 400 { code: "INVALID_REPORT_RANGE" }
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

POST {{base}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "reportType": "SALES_SUMMARY", "format": "XLSX", "from": "2000-01-01", "to": "2025-01-01" }


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### VALIDATION — extra property (forbidNonWhitelisted). Expect: 400
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

POST {{base}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "reportType": "SALES_SUMMARY", "format": "XLSX", "evil": "payload" }


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### FORBIDDEN — a cashier has no report access. Expect: 403
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

POST {{base}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}

{ "reportType": "SALES_SUMMARY", "format": "XLSX" }


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### UNAUTHORIZED — missing token. Expect: 401
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

GET {{base}}/reports


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### LIST REPORT JOBS (paged). Admins see every job; pharmacists see their own.
### Optional filters: reportType, status, page, pageSize
### status: QUEUED | PROCESSING | COMPLETED | FAILED
### Expect: 200 + { data, total, page, pageSize, totalPages } (result_data never
###         appears in the list projection).
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# @name listReports
GET {{base}}/reports?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### LIST FILTERED — only COMPLETED sales reports
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

GET {{base}}/reports?reportType=SALES_SUMMARY&status=COMPLETED
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### GET ONE REPORT JOB STATUS
### Expect: 200 + job DTO; 404 if unknown or if it belongs to another user.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

GET {{base}}/reports/{{jobId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### DOWNLOAD A COMPLETED REPORT (authenticated — this is what the SPA calls,
### since it has the Bearer token in memory).
### Expect: 200 + file bytes (Content-Disposition: attachment)
###         410 Gone if the job is not COMPLETED or the file has expired.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

GET {{base}}/reports/{{jobId}}/download
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### DOWNLOAD VIA THE SIGNED EMAIL LINK (public — no Authorization header).
### The :token is the `<uuid>.<expiryEpochMs>.<hmac>` string embedded in the
### report email's "Descargar mi reporte" link. Paste one here to replay it.
### This route works from any machine (host comes from REPORT_DOWNLOAD_BASE_URL)
### and needs no session token; a tampered/expired token returns 404.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

GET {{base}}/reports/d/{{signedToken}}


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### SSE STREAM — push notifications for report completions (2nd channel).
### The server filters events to your own jobs (admins receive all).
### Expect: 200 text/event-stream; keep the request open and complete a QUEUED
###         report to see a `report.completed` / `report.failed` event.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

GET {{base}}/reports/stream
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: text/event-stream


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### END-TO-END WORKED EXAMPLE (PMS-014 async happy path)
###   1. Send "Login as Admin".
###   2. Send "ASYNC REPORT — large range" → copy .body.id into @jobId.
###   3. Poll "GET ONE REPORT JOB STATUS" until status = COMPLETED
###      (the in-process worker drains the queue; watch the SSE stream too).
###   4. Send "DOWNLOAD A COMPLETED REPORT" → you get the xlsx bytes.
###   5. Check your inbox: the "Descargar mi reporte" link contains the signed
###      token — paste it into @signedToken and use the public download route
###      to confirm it works with NO Authorization header.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
